    {
      "id": "claim_877bd2f020264f16a4faad45fddefb18",
      "statement": "Every mark mutation (addHighlight, setMarkComment, setMarkColor, removeMark, linkMarkToField, unlinkMarkFromField) pushes its own undo step in the Zustand store; setMarkComment coalesces consecutive keystrokes via lastFieldKey, and comment/color/link/unlink changes propagate to every fragment sharing a groupId so a cross-page highlight behaves as one logical mark. unlinkMarkFromField deletes linkedFields back to undefined once the last link is removed so a never-linked mark round-trips byte-identical.",
      "evidence": [
