    {
      "id": "claim_74dc993787ff4b038ba39a426ba13d87",
      "statement": "PdfViewer mounts one react-pdf Page element per page with no virtualization, each with its own canvas/text/annotation layer and pageRefs entry. onLoadSuccess caps the mounted count at MAX_PDF_PAGES (5000) and records overflow in truncatedPages, because a hostile 2.4 KB PDF whose page tree is a DAG can claim 16 million pages and crash the renderer. Page elements are memoized and the onRenderTextLayerSuccess callback is a stable useCallback so unrelated re-renders keep pdf.js text layers intact.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/PdfViewer.tsx#L1333-L1333",
