    {
      "id": "claim_39a1d464cee04a40b394d127a20bab06",
      "statement": "pdfText.ts extractPdfText produces full plain text one [page N] block per page for pasting into an LLM prompt instead of uploading the PDF. linesFromItems mirrors pdfMeta's baseline-bucketing layout heuristic (duplicated, not imported, to keep the module independent) because pdf.js does not promise items in reading order. A single bad page is skipped; only a document that can't be opened throws. Extraction is capped at DEFAULT_MAX_PAGES (2000) since page count is file-controlled and an uncapped walk would freeze; the empty flag (body chars < 200, excluding page markers) marks a scanned/image-only PDF so the AI flow can fall back.",
